        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alma Wade\n- Products: F.E.A.R., SAS: Secure Tomorrow\n- Companies: Monolith Productions, Sierra Entertainment\n- Systems: Jupiter EX engine\n- Concepts: survival horror, first-person shooter, series mystery\n\nFacts:\n- In 2005, Monolith Productions introduced Alma Wade in F.E.A.R. as a major antagonist and key figure in the F.E.A.R. series of first-person shooter horror video games.\n- Alma Wade is the central mystery at the core of the F.E.A.R. series.\n- F.E.A.R. First Encounter Assault Recon is a survival horror first-person shooter video game developed by Monolith Productions and published by Sierra Entertainment.\n- SAS: Secure Tomorrow uses the Jupiter EX engine, which is similar or possibly identical to the engine used in F.E.A.R..",
